  "summary": "Kolhapuri chappals or Kolhapuris are Indian hand-crafted, braided leather slip-on sandals that are locally tanned using vegetable dyes, and hand-decorated with patterns.",
  "description": "Kolhapuri chappals or Kolhapuris are Indian hand-crafted, braided leather slip-on sandals that are locally tanned using vegetable dyes, and hand-decorated with patterns. They are open-toed, T-strap sandals with a loop to hold the big toe, and a large foot loop forward of the ankle fixed by a cord to an attachment point near the toe loop, made to slip on without any fastening. Braided leather Mules or braided leather shoe type designs are also common.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Maharashtra, Karnataka; registration 2018–19), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
